A stop moves every thread it stops back by a call, the ready ones too,
so one stopped between two instructions runs again from an instruction before,
and one that stops itself makes its stop again once resumed:
a thread stops where it stood.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a stop moved a thread from where it stood

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -454,8 +454,8 @@ static bool thread_stop(struct thread *t)
 {
     if (t->state == THREAD_WAITING) {
         unwait(t);
-        t->frame.pc -= CALL_SIZE;
     }
+    t->frame.pc -= CALL_SIZE;
     t->state = THREAD_STOPPED;
     return core_thread_stopped(t);
 }
